    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0330" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>

                <p>And this deponent, Samuel Mullins, on his oath, saith:</p>
                <p>I am a solicitor at 11 Queen Victoria street, E. C. I was present at the
                    examination of prisoner before Sir Thomas Henry in March last. A draft was
                    produced for the sum of $15,000; that draft was annexed to the original
                    documents which came from America; these documents, with the draft, have been
                    sent back to New York.</p>
                <p>In the presence of prisoner I heard the American depositions read in which Mr.
                    Warren, who purported to have signed the check or draft, said his signature was
                    a forgery.</p>
                <closer><signed>SAMUEL MULLINS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The above depositions of John Shore and Samuel Mullins were severally taken
                        and sworn before me as aforesaid.</p>
                    <p rendition="#right">J. T. INGHAM,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief
                            Magistrate.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
